WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.870
In a café, Sam orders: Quiero un café.

2
00:00:03.920 --> 00:00:06.210
Lucía orders: Quisiera un café.

3
00:00:06.260 --> 00:00:09.190
You know Lucía's version
is the polite one.

4
00:00:09.240 --> 00:00:13.350
But quisiera is more
than a polite phrase.

5
00:00:13.400 --> 00:00:16.390
It belongs to a whole verb form
you'll meet when you read and

6
00:00:16.440 --> 00:00:17.250
listen.

7
00:00:17.300 --> 00:00:20.970
So when you meet a line
like Si tuviera tiempo…

8
00:00:21.020 --> 00:00:22.610
, what does it mean?

9
00:00:22.660 --> 00:00:26.230
In this mission, you'll meet
the imperfect subjunctive.

10
00:00:26.280 --> 00:00:28.980
You only need to recognise
it, not build it.

11
00:00:29.030 --> 00:00:30.630
You'll spot it by its look,

12
00:00:30.680 --> 00:00:34.610
and see the kind of verb that
follows it in the same sentence.

13
00:00:34.660 --> 00:00:37.970
Your mission: work out
what Si tuviera tiempo…

14
00:00:38.020 --> 00:00:39.930
really means.
